# Retail data (port/docs/retail-eu-plan.md): the European rooms' difficulty branches this build lacks (read
# with retail_code.py and the modules' relocations; game_country is the difficulty class, patch 0140).
# r203 (st2_0.rel R203Init): their data put a message area 6 ("locked") at etc door 5; above Easy it is off,
# on Easy door 5 stays locked, the door to r201 needs no key and neither the three wandering Ganados nor the
# key carrier's group come (this build kept area 6 on Normal at an open door). r211 (st2_2.rel R211Init): on
# Easy the first cup is in place and model group 0x20 shows with its collision (room archive entry 5), above
# Easy group 0x20 is off (this build showed it without collision). Map screen (Sscrn.rel, mapAreaFilename):
# on Easy the map objects come from SS/Esy. Nothing changes with the debug build's discs. A port patch for
# retail data.
